    basic: 'As declarer, lead with your strong combinations to shed cards quickly. As the secret partner, help the declarer without revealing yourself too early — play high cards to support their leads.',
    intermediate: 'Partner revelation timing: revealing early doubles the score but makes you a target. Reveal late only if winning is certain. As an opponent, watch for suspicious play that suggests someone is helping the declarer.',
    advanced: "Bomb management: holding a bomb gives you enormous power to interrupt opponents' leads. Save bombs for critical moments when opponents are about to go out. Social deduction: track which players pass on beatable combinations — they may be secretly helping the declarer.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Don't expose both Aces immediately unless you have an extremely strong hand for solo play.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "As the secret partner, subtle cooperation (not trumping the declarer's leads, helping clear their suits) is more valuable than flashy reveals.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Bomb timing is everything: playing a bomb too early wastes your best interruption tool.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Pay attention to card counts: know who has few cards left and prioritize stopping them.',
